-- selfroute: a module that reroutes its OWN error stream from within
-- (§13.14). It writes `reroute Error Tmp` — both arguments mangle
-- (§13.13), so the install is Error_v2 → Tmp_v2: the module-wide
-- reroute of its own error stream to one of its own bags (its written
-- `Error` IS its own mangled error bag — it cannot name the real
-- top-level Error, consistent with the no-Global-exemption story).
-- Its own Tmp handler block (mangled like everything else) catches
-- the rerouted tuples there, keyed on the tag Error_v2 — the tag
-- stays the original mangled Error bag: stable provenance (§13.14).
: [reroute Error Tmp; (Ready,)]

(Boom, reply) : error ("bad", reply)

Tmp { (Error, msg, reply) : lob reply (Caught, msg) }
